title: The Death of DuFour
subtitle: The President has died...
new-page: true
view-if: year = 1934 and month >= 7 and president = "DuFour" and gnu_formed
on-arrival: {!
for (var c of Q.classes) {
    var class_votes = 0;
    for (var party of Q.parties) {
        if (Q[c+'_'+party] < 0) {
            Q[c+'_'+party] = 0;
        }
        class_votes += Q[c+'_'+party];
    }
    for (var party of Q.parties) {
        Q[c + '_' + party + '_normalized'] = 100*Q[c+'_'+party]/class_votes;
        Q[c + '_' + party + '_display'] = Math.round(100*Q[c+'_'+party]/class_votes);
    }
}
// calculate support for each of the parties
var total_support = 0; 
for (var party of Q.parties) {
    var party_support = 0;
    for (var c of Q.classes) {
        if (Q.old_demographics) { 
            party_support += Q[c]*Q[c+'_'+party];
        } else  { 
            party_support += Q[c]*Q[c+'_'+party+'_normalized'];
        } 
    }
    Q[party + '_support'] = party_support;
    total_support += party_support; 
    if (party == "royalist" && Q.royalist_split) {
        Q.royalist_gallax_support = Q.landed_royalist_normalized*Q.landed;
        Q.royalist_gallax_support += Q.guild_royalist_normalized*Q.guild;
        Q.royalist_gallax_support += Q.faithful_royalist_normalized*Q.faithful;

        if (Q.dsu_exist && !Q.nvf_exist) {
            Q.dsu_support = Q.commons_royalist*Q.commons*((120 - Q.loyalist_force) / 100);
            Q.dsu_support += Q.disfavored_royalist*Q.disfavored*((80 - Q.loyalist_force) / 100);
            Q.dsu_support += Q.burgher_royalist*Q.burgher;
        } else if (!Q.dsu_exist && Q.nvf_exist) {
            Q.nvf_support = Q.disfavored_royalist*Q.disfavored*((120 - Q.loyalist_force) / 100);
            Q.nvf_support += Q.commons_royalist*Q.commons*((Q.loyalist_force - 80) / 100);
            Q.nvf_support += Q.burgher_royalist*Q.burgher;
        } else if (Q.dsu_exist && Q.nvf_exist) {
            Q.dsu_support = Q.commons_royalist*Q.commons*((120 - Q.loyalist_force) / 100);
            Q.dsu_support += Q.disfavored_royalist*Q.disfavored*((80 - Q.loyalist_force) / 100);
            Q.dsu_support += Q.burgher_royalist*Q.burgher;

            Q.nvf_support = Q.disfavored_royalist*Q.disfavored*((120 - Q.loyalist_force) / 100);
            Q.nvf_support += Q.commons_royalist*Q.commons*((Q.loyalist_force - 80) / 100);
        } else {
            Q.royalist_gallax_support += Q.commons_royalist*Q.commons;
            Q.royalist_gallax_support += Q.disfavored_royalist*Q.disfavored;
            Q.royalist_gallax_support += Q.burgher_royalist*Q.burgher;
        }
    }
}
// 2. normalize support (fraction)
for (var party of Q.parties) {
    Q[party+'_normalized'] = Q[party + '_support']/total_support;
    if (party == "royalist" && Q.royalist_split) {
        Q.royalist_gallax_normalized = Q.royalist_gallax_support / total_support;
        Q.dsu_normalized = Q.dsu_support / total_support;
        Q.nvf_normalized = Q.nvf_support / total_support;
        Q.royalist_gallax_votes = Math.round(Q.royalist_gallax_normalized*1000) / 10;
        Q.dsu_votes = Math.round(Q.dsu_normalized*1000) / 10;
        Q.nvf_votes = Math.round(Q.nvf_normalized*1000) / 10;
    }
    Q[party+'_votes'] = Math.round(Q[party+'_normalized']*1000)/ 10;
}

Q.round = 0;
Q.dufour_dead = 1;
Q.president = "Bumke (acting)";
if (Q.judicial_reform >= 4) Q.president = "Großmann (acting)"

Q.Heuss_votes_pre = 0;

Q.gnu_candidate = "Hammerton";
Q.marcher_candidate = "Shackley";
Q.collectivist_candidate = Q.marcher_candidate;
Q.unionist_candidate = "Aldermoor";
if (Q.unionist_leader == "Hughes") Q.unionist_candidate = Q.gnu_candidate;
Q.ddp_candidate = "Hewes";
Q.lvp_candidate = "Hewes";
Q.gold_candidate = "Hewes";
if (Q.dstp_gnu) Q.ddp_candidate = Q.gnu_candidate;
if (Q.lvp_gnu) Q.lvp_candidate = Q.gnu_candidate;
if (Q.gold_gnu) Q.gold_candidate = Q.gnu_candidate;
Q.heuss_run = 1;
if (Q.ddp_candidate == "Hewes") Q.Heuss_votes_pre += Q.ddp_votes;
if (Q.lvp_candidate == "Hewes") Q.Heuss_votes_pre += Q.lvp_votes;
if (Q.gold_candidate == "Hewes") Q.Heuss_votes_pre += Q.gold_votes;
if (Q.Heuss_votes_pre < 8) {
    if (Q.unionist_candidate != Q.gnu_candidate) Q.ddp_candidate = Q.unionist_candidate;
    if (Q.unionist_candidate != Q.gnu_candidate) Q.lvp_candidate = Q.unionist_candidate;
    if (Q.unionist_candidate != Q.gnu_candidate) Q.gold_candidate = Q.unionist_candidate;
    if (Q.unionist_candidate == Q.gnu_candidate) Q.ddp_candidate = Q.gnu_candidate;
    if (Q.unionist_candidate == Q.gnu_candidate) Q.lvp_candidate = Q.gnu_candidate;
    if (Q.unionist_candidate == Q.gnu_candidate) Q.gold_candidate = Q.gnu_candidate;
    if (Q.dstp_gnu) Q.ddp_candidate = Q.gnu_candidate;
    if (Q.lvp_gnu) Q.lvp_candidate = Q.gnu_candidate;
    if (Q.gold_gnu) Q.gold_candidate = Q.gnu_candidate;
    Q.heuss_run = 0;
}
Q.royalist_candidate = "Gorrick";
Q.royalist_gallax_candidate = "Gorrick";
if (Q.dsu_leader != "Otto Crowde") Q.dsu_candidate = "Frask";
if (Q.dsu_leader == "Otto Crowde") Q.dsu_candidate = "Crowde";
Q.nvf_candidate = "Boycott";
if (Q.nvf_gnu) Q.nvf_candidate = "Hammerton";
Q.traditionalist_candidate = "Hammerton";
Q.other_candidate = "Hammerton";
Q.is_unity_candidate = 0;
Q.sapd_candidate = Q.collectivist_candidate;
Q.kvp_candidate = Q.traditionalist_candidate;
Q.dnf_candidate = Q.traditionalist_candidate;
!}
max-visits: 1
on-display: {!  
    var cardEl = document.createElement('div');  
    cardEl.className = "face-figure2";  

    var image = new Image();  
    image.className = "face-img";  
    image.src = "img/DuFour_head.jpg";  

    cardEl.appendChild(image);  
    var contentDiv = document.querySelector("#page #mid_panel #content");
    contentDiv.appendChild(cardEl);
!}
tags: event

= The Death of DuFour

President Paul von DuFour has passed away at age 86. An era of history is closing, and the future remains to be seen.

The nation erupts in grief over the death of its war hero and president—though this mourning is confined largely to the political right. With Staal not expected to live much longer, the era of the Commonwealth's two strongmen nears its end. Now, the country must determine who will author the next chapter of the Unity Republic—if it will still be called that.

New presidential elections are to be held as soon as possible. The <span style="color: #BFC8CC;">**GNU**</span> is expected to field a single candidate, and their victory would guarantee a total consolidation of power for the foreseeable future—an outcome that must be prevented at all costs. In the meantime, Supreme Court chief justice [? if judicial_reform < 4 : Erwin Bumke ?][? if judicial_reform >= 4 : Hermann Großmann ?] serves as the acting president.

- @candidates: Who are the candidates so far?

@candidates

The <span style="color: #BFC8CC;">**GNU**</span> has nominated Kurt von Hammerton-Equord—a Commonwealth Army general, long-time friend of Staal, and the current Chief of the Army. He considers himself a servant of the state rather than of any political party, and served as Staal’s liaison to the trade unions in recent months. He has also been responsible for overseeing the expansion of the Commonwealth Army during this time. Little else is known about his ideological convictions; like Staal, he is flexible.

- @candidates_nazis

@candidates_nazis
title: The <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalist</span>'s last hurrah?

With Gallax gone from the political scene, the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalists</span> will be fielding Ulric Gorrick as their candidate.

The <span style="color: #6A1E1E;">**DSU**</span> will be running [? if dsu_candidate == "Crowde": their party leader, Otto Crowde, as a separate candidate. ?][? if dsu_candidate == "Frask": Wilhelm Frask as a separate candidate. ?]

[? if nvf_candidate == gnu_candidate: The remnants of the <span style="color: #142e20;">**NVF**</span> will be backing [+ gnu_candidate +], as they remain within the <span style="color: #BFC8CC;">**GNU**</span> umbrella. ?][? if nvf_candidate != gnu_candidate: The remnants of the <span style="color: #142e20;">**NVF**</span> will be boycotting the election entirely—continuing their deluded course of waiting for the "right moment" to spark an armed rebellion. ?]

With the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalists</span> movement remaining divided, none of their candidates have any remote chance to winning.

- @candidates_nats

@candidates_nats
title: Moving on to the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">nationalists</span>.

The <span style="color: #3E88B3;">nationalists</span> are unified in their support for [+ gnu_candidate +], joined by the various splinter factions and the minor bourgeois parties. Although Mallin is—somehow—still contemplating a presidential run, a strongly worded threat has convinced him to remain silent.

- @candidates_dems

@candidates_dems
title: The <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span>? The Unity Parties? Who will they support?

With the <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span> having been heavily suppressed during Staal’s tenure, they are no longer a significant political force. [? if collectivist_banned: They are even banned outright, preventing them from endorsing their own candidate. With boycotting rendered pointless, they have no choice but to support whoever we put forward. ?][? if not collectivist_banned: Grateful for our role in sparing them from Staal’s crackdown months ago, they are fully backing whoever we choose to nominate. ?]

[? if unionist_candidate == "Aldermoor": The <span style="color: #000000;">Unionists</span> is not fully convinced to back [+ gnu_candidate +] and has chosen to run its own candidate: Konrad Aldermoor. The Mayor of Bradford since the Republic's inception, and a member of the Heartland legislature, he's an advocate for the <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span> "leaving the tower" to broaden its appeal among Protestants, Aldermoor was first proposed by Sedgewick himself. Though situated on the right wing of his party, he remains firmly committed to the Unity Republic and opposes Staal’s threats against it. ?]

[? if heuss_run: The <span style="color: #FFCC00;">liberals</span> are running Theodor Hewes—a journalist and vocal supporter of the Unity Republic, and a staunch anti-Staalist within his own party. This stance has put him at odds with more pro-Staal elements in the Commonwealth middle class. While unlikely to secure significant support, Hewes has positioned himself as a "Unity" unity candidate in opposition to [+ gnu_candidate +]. ?][? if not heuss_run and ddp_candidate == unionist_candidate and unionist_candidate != gnu_candidate: The <span style="color: #FFCC00;">liberals</span>, mired in electoral ruin, lack the resources or energy to field a candidate of their own. Instead, they have thrown their support behind [+ unionist_candidate +] as the bourgeois alternative to Staal. However, their backing is far from solid—pro-Staal elements remain rogue, as his message of national solidarity continues to resonate with the historically nationalist Commonwealth liberal movement. ?][? if not heuss_run and ddp_candidate == gnu_candidate: The <span style="color: #FFCC00;">liberals</span>, mired in electoral ruin, lack the resources or energy to field a candidate of their own. They have thrown their support behind [+ gnu_candidate +], heavily influenced by pro-Staal elements and propaganda that has resonated especially strongly with their rank-and-file. Many within the party now see it as their national duty to support Staal and his successor, believing this to be the only path toward restoring the Commonwealth’s great power status abroad and securing concessions at home. ?]

- @candidates_spd

@candidates_spd
title: Finally, what about us?
go-to: candidate_menu

As for the <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span>, we could support a joint Unity Coalition candidate or run our own. The viability of a united front, however, depends entirely on our relations with former coalition partners—and whether they’ve fallen under Staal’s influence.

Lyle Bristol is tired. He ran and failed in the previous two presidential elections, and no longer wishes to run. His wife is ill enough that he wishes to stay by her side.  More importantly, he is deeply pessimistic about the situation we now face.

Kurt Shackley is an ambitious rising star in the party, and would be all too willing to run. He was a hero in the Great War, but his relatively young age might be relevant.

@candidate_menu

- @hammerstein_r1: Support the <span style="color: #BFC8CC;">**GNU**</span>'s [+ gnu_candidate +].
- @adenauer_r1: Support Konrad Aldermoor of the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?].
- @heuss_r1: Support Theodor Hewes of the [? if not lvp_formed: <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span>?][? if lvp_formed: <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>?].
- @schumacher_r1: Run Kurt Shackley.
- @abstain: Do nothing.

@abstain
view-if: resources < 2
on-arrival: marcher_candidate = "Boycott"; collectivist_candidate = "Boycott"; sapd_candidate = "Boycott"
go-to: r1_menu

What an anticlimactic way to go.

- @round_1: Let the voting begin.

@hammerstein_r1
unavailable-subtitle: We are a democratic party. 
choose-if: staal_marcher_influence >= 8
on-arrival: marcher_candidate = gnu_candidate; collectivist_candidate = "Boycott"; sapd_candidate = "Boycott"
go-to: r1_menu

I hope you had a reason in mind.

- @round_1: Let the voting begin.

@adenauer_r1
view-if: unionist_candidate == "Aldermoor"
on-arrival: marcher_candidate = "Aldermoor"; collectivist_candidate = "Boycott"; sapd_candidate = "Boycott"; unionist_relation += 5; center_bvp_votes = 1 if unionist_relation < 50; is_unity_candidate = 1
go-to: r1_menu

We have endorsed Konrad Aldermoor of the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?]. Perhaps we can form a Unity Bloc against Staal.

[? if unionist_relation < 50 : With our support of Aldermoor, some of the most conservative parts of the <span style="color: #A2D8E0;">the Arcanists</span> have broken away from the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?], shifting their support to [+ gnu_candidate +]. Hopefully it doesn't lead to a repeat of the 4290 Presidential election. ?]

@heuss_r1
view-if: heuss_run
on-arrival: marcher_candidate = "Hewes"; collectivist_candidate = "Boycott"; sapd_candidate = "Boycott"; ddp_relation += 8; lvp_relation += 5; gold_candidate = gnu_candidate if gold_relation < 60 and gold_candidate == marcher_candidate and gold_exist and not lvp_formed; is_unity_candidate = 1
go-to: r1_menu

We have endorsed Theodor Hewes, journalist of the [? if not lvp_formed: <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span>?][? if lvp_formed: 
<span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>?]. Perhaps we can form a Unity Bloc against Staal.

[? if gold_relation < 60 and gold_candidate == marcher_candidate and gold_exist and not lvp_formed: With our support of Hewes, the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span> components supporting him have broken away and are now supporting [+ gnu_candidate +] if they haven't already. ?]

@schumacher_r1
subtitle: -2 resources.
unavailable-subtitle: [? if resources < 2 : -2 resources - Not enough resources. ?]
choose-if: resources >= 2
on-arrival: marcher_candidate = "Shackley"; resources -= 2; is_unity_candidate = 0
go-to: r1_menu

We have nominated Kurt Shackley to be our presidential candidate. However, convincing the Unity parties—many of which have shifted significantly to the right—to openly support a <span style="color: #c00000;">Reformist</span> will be no easy task.

@r1_menu
view-if: round = 0

- @convince_z_unity
- @convince_z_spd
- @convince_lvp_spd
- @convince_lvp_unity
- @convince_ddp_spd
- @convince_ddp_unity
- @convince_dvp_unity
- @round_1: Let the voting begin.


# convincing Z to support a unity candidate
@convince_z_unity
title: Convince the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] to support [+ marcher_candidate +].
view-if: marcher_candidate = "Hewes" and unionist_candidate != marcher_candidate
on-arrival: {!
Q.unionist_support_braun = 0;
if (Q.unionist_relation >= 60 || (Q.unionist_relation > 50 && Q.unionist_ideology == "Left")) {
    Q.unionist_support_braun = 1;
} else if (Q.unionist_relation < 35) {
    Q.unionist_support_braun = 0;
} else {
    Q.unionist_support_braun = 2;
}
if (Q.unionist_candidate == Q.gnu_candidate) Q.unionist_support_braun = 0;
!}
max-visits: 1
go-to: z_failed if unionist_support_braun = 0 or (unionist_support_braun == 2 and historical_mode); z_success if unionist_support_braun = 1; z_partial if unionist_support_braun = 2 and not historical_mode

We implore the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] to support [+ marcher_candidate +] as a unity candidate against Staal, arguing that together, the Unity Coalition can defeat the <span style="color: #BFC8CC;">**GNU**</span>. [? if unionist_relation >= 50 : We also remind them of the history of cooperation between our parties, dating back to 4283. ?]

@convince_z_spd
title: Convince the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] to support [+ marcher_candidate +].
choose-if: marcher_votes >= unionist_votes
unavailable-subtitle: [? if marcher_votes < unionist_votes: The [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionists</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] knows that they are more popular than us; they do not see a reason to support our candidate. ?]
view-if: marcher_candidate == "Shackley" and unionist_candidate != marcher_candidate
on-arrival: {!
Q.unionist_support_braun = 0;
if (Q.unionist_relation >= 75 || (Q.unionist_relation > 65 && Q.unionist_ideology == "Left")) {
    Q.unionist_support_braun = 1;
} else if (Q.unionist_relation < 55) {
    Q.unionist_support_braun = 0;
} else {
    Q.unionist_support_braun = 2;
}
if (Q.unionist_candidate == Q.gnu_candidate) Q.unionist_support_braun = 0;
!}
max-visits: 1
go-to: z_failed if unionist_support_braun = 0 or (unionist_support_braun == 2 and historical_mode); z_success if unionist_support_braun = 1; z_partial if unionist_support_braun = 2 and not historical_mode

We implore the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] to support [+ marcher_candidate +]. We attempt to convince them of the necessity for unity in the face of Staal's dictatorial aspirations: that if we were divided, we would fall under influence of the <span style="color: #BFC8CC;">**GNU**</span>. [? if unionist_relation >= 50 : We also remind them of the history of cooperation between our parties, dating back to 4283. ?]

@z_failed
go-to: r1_menu if round = 0; r2_campaigning if round > 0

Unfortunately, the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] is not convinced. [? if unionist_candidate == gnu_candidate : This is hardly surprising—they’ve become a <i>Blocpartei</i> at this point.  ?]

@z_success
on-arrival: unionist_candidate = marcher_candidate; center_bvp_votes = 1 if unionist_relation < 50; gold_candidate_switch = 1 if gold_candidate != gnu_candidate and gold_candidate == marcher_candidate; gold_candidate = gnu_candidate if gold_candidate == marcher_candidate
go-to: r1_menu if round = 0; r2_campaigning if round > 0

The [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] is convinced! They will be supporting [+ marcher_candidate +] for the election.

[? if unionist_relation < 50 : With our support of Aldermoor, some of the most conservative parts of the <span style="color: #A2D8E0;">the Arcanists</span> have broken away from the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?], shifting their support to [+ gnu_candidate +]. Hopefully it doesn't lead to a repeat of the 4290 Presidential election. ?]

[? if gold_candidate_switch: The <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span> have also switched to supporting [+ gnu_candidate +] as they're heavily uncomfortable with being on the same side as us. ?]

@z_partial

The [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionists</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] are not satisfied with our arguments, but they are open to being convinced. They are willing to run a joint campaign if we front the resources.

- @pay_z: Give them the resources they need.
- @r1_menu: Forget about the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionists</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?].
- @r2_campaigning: Forget about the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionists</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?].

@pay_z
choose-if: resources >= 2
subtitle: -2 resources
on-arrival: resources -= 2; unionist_candidate = marcher_candidate; center_bvp_votes = 1 if unionist_relation < 50
go-to: r1_menu if round = 0; r2_campaigning if round > 0

With our resources, the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionists</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] are convinced to support [+ marcher_candidate +]. Konrad Aldermoor will drop out of the race.

[? if unionist_relation < 50 : With our support of Aldermoor, some of the most conservative parts of the <span style="color: #A2D8E0;">the Arcanists</span> have broken away from the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?], shifting their support to [+ gnu_candidate +]. Hopefully it doesn't lead to a repeat of the 4290 Presidential election. ?]


@convince_ddp_unity
title: Convince the <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span> to support [+ marcher_candidate +].
view-if: marcher_candidate = "Aldermoor" and ddp_candidate != marcher_candidate and not lvp_formed
on-arrival: ddp_candidate = marcher_candidate if ddp_relation >= 40 and not dstp_gnu
go-to: r1_menu if round = 0; r2_campaigning if round > 0
max-visits: 1

[? if ddp_candidate = marcher_candidate: The <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span> is easily persuaded to support [+ marcher_candidate +]! This is largely because [+ marcher_candidate +] is the candidate of the <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>, not of the <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span>. ?]
[? if ddp_candidate != marcher_candidate: Unfortunately, the <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span> is unwilling to support [+ marcher_candidate +]. The Unity Coalition seems to be fracturing with Staal undoubtedly playing a role. ?]


@convince_ddp_spd
title: Convince the <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span> to support [+ marcher_candidate +].
view-if: marcher_candidate = "Shackley" and ddp_candidate != marcher_candidate and not lvp_formed
on-arrival: ddp_candidate = marcher_candidate if ((ddp_relation >= 50 and unionist_relation >= 60) or (ddp_relation >= 60 and unionist_relation < 60)) and not dstp_gnu
go-to: r1_menu if round = 0; r2_campaigning if round > 0
max-visits: 1

[? if ddp_candidate = marcher_candidate: The <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span> is easily persuaded to support [+ marcher_candidate +], convinced by our argument that his election is the last line of defense for democracy against Staal. ?]
[? if ddp_candidate != marcher_candidate: Unfortunately, the <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span> is unwilling to support [+ marcher_candidate +]. Somewhat expectedly considering he's a <span style="color: #c00000;">Reformist</span>. ?]

@convince_lvp_spd
title: Convince the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span> to support [+ marcher_candidate +].
view-if: marcher_candidate = "Shackley" and lvp_candidate != marcher_candidate and lvp_formed
on-arrival: lvp_candidate = marcher_candidate if ((lvp_relation >= 55 and unionist_relation >= 60) or (lvp_relation >= 65 and unionist_relation < 60)) and not lvp_gnu
go-to: r1_menu if round = 0; r2_campaigning if round > 0
max-visits: 1

[? if lvp_candidate = marcher_candidate: The <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span> is reluctantly persuaded to support [+ marcher_candidate +], convinced by our argument that his election is the last line of defense for democracy against Staal. ?]
[? if lvp_candidate != marcher_candidate: Unfortunately, the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span> is unwilling to support [+ marcher_candidate +]—expected, given he's a <span style="color: #c00000;">Reformist</span>, and that we're asking the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span> in the first place. ?]

@convince_lvp_unity
title: Convince the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span> to support [+ marcher_candidate +].
view-if: marcher_candidate = "Aldermoor" and lvp_candidate != marcher_candidate and lvp_formed
on-arrival: lvp_candidate = marcher_candidate if lvp_relation >= 45 and not lvp_gnu
go-to: r1_menu if round = 0; r2_campaigning if round > 0
max-visits: 1

[? if lvp_candidate = marcher_candidate:  The <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span> is reluctantly persuaded to support [+ marcher_candidate +]! This is largely because [+ marcher_candidate +] is the candidate of the <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>, not of the <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span>. ?]
[? if lvp_candidate != marcher_candidate: Unfortunately, the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span> is unwilling to support [+ marcher_candidate +]. The Unity Coalition seems to be fracturing with Staal undoubtedly playing a role. ?]

@convince_dvp_unity
title: Convince the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span> to support [+ marcher_candidate +].
subtitle: [? if marcher_candidate = ddp_candidate and not gold_gnu: The <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span> are uncomfortable in participating on the same side as the <span style="color: #c00000;">Reformists</span>. ?]
unavailable-subtitle: The <span style="color: #C0A054;">Golds</span> is not willing to support our candidate.
view-if: (marcher_candidate = "Aldermoor" or marcher_candidate = "Hewes") and gold_candidate != marcher_candidate and not gold_gnu and not lvp_formed
choose-if: gold_relation >= 60 and gold_leader != "Dingeldey" and gold_ideology != "Right"
on-arrival: gold_candidate = marcher_candidate; gold_relation += 5; gold_left += 1; gold_candidate_switch = 1 if gold_candidate != gnu_candidate and gold_candidate == marcher_candidate; gold_candidate = gnu_candidate if gold_candidate == marcher_candidate
go-to: r1_menu if round = 0; r2_campaigning if round > 0
max-visits: 1

[? if gold_candidate = marcher_candidate: Thanks to our good relations, and the fact that our candidate is a unity candidate not affiliated with the <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span>, the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span> is persuaded to support [+ marcher_candidate +]. ?]

[? if gold_candidate_switch: The <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span> have also switched to supporting [+ gnu_candidate +] as they're heavily uncomfortable with being on the same side as us. ?]

@round_1
go-to: election_algorithm
set-jump: post_election


@post_election
on-arrival: {!
var candidate_descs = {
  Crowde: "Otto Crowde of the <span style='color: #6A1E1E; font-weight: bold;'>DSU</span>",
  Frask: "Wilhelm Frask of the <span style='color: #6A1E1E; font-weight: bold;'>DSU</span>",
  Gorrick: "Ulric Gorrick of the <span style='color: #7A3C00; font-weight: bold;'>Royalists</span>",
  Hammerton: "Kurt von Hammerton-Equord of the <span style='color: #BFC8CC; font-weight: bold;'>GNU</span>",
  Aldermoor: "Konrad Aldermoor of the <span style='color: #000000; font-weight: bold;'>Unionist Party</span>",
  Hewes: "Theodor Hewes of the <span style='color: #D3C24D; font-weight: bold;'>Golds</span>",
  Shackley: "Kurt Shackley of the <span style='color: #c00000; font-weight: bold;'>Marchers</span>"
};

if (Q.dstp_formed) {
    candidate_descs.Hewes = "Theodor Hewes of the <span style='color: #D3C24D; font-weight: bold;'>DStP</span>";
}
if (Q.lvp_formed) {
    candidate_descs.Hewes = "Theodor Hewes of the <span style='color: #C0A054; font-weight: bold;'>Golds</span>";
}
if (Q.unionist_party_name == "Concord") {
    candidate_descs.Aldermoor = "Konrad Aldermoor of the <span style='color: #000000; font-weight: bold;'>Concord</span>";
}
for (var k in candidate_descs) {
    Q[k + '_running'] = 0;
}
var candidate_votes = {};
Q.parties_election = Q.parties;
if (Q.dsu_exist) {
    Q.parties_election.push('royalist_gallax');
    Q.parties_election.push('dsu');
    Q.royalist_normalized = 0;
}
if (Q.nvf_exist) {
    Q.parties_election.push('nvf');
    Q.royalist_normalized -= Q.nvf_normalized;
    Q.royalist_normalized = 0;
}
if (Q.center_bvp_votes) {
    Q.bvp_normalized = Q.bvp_votes / 100;
    Q.unionist_normalized -= Q.bvp_normalized;
    Q.parties_election.push('bvp')
    Q.bvp_candidate = Q.gnu_candidate;
}
for (var party of Q.parties_election) {
    var supported_candidate = Q[party + '_candidate'];
    supported_candidate = supported_candidate.normalize("NFD").replace(/[\u0300-\u036f]/g, "");
    Q[supported_candidate + '_running'] = 1;
    if (supported_candidate in candidate_votes) {
        candidate_votes[supported_candidate] += Q[party + '_normalized'];
    } else {
        candidate_votes[supported_candidate] = Q[party + '_normalized'];
    }
}
var total_votes = 0;
Q.winner = "";  
Q.winner_votes = 0;
Q.has_majority = 0;
for (var k in candidate_votes) {
    total_votes += candidate_votes[k];
    if (candidate_votes[k] > Q.winner_votes) {
        Q.winner = k;
        Q.winner_votes = candidate_votes[k];
    }
    if (candidate_votes[k] >= 0.5) {
        Q.has_majority = 1;
    }
}
for (var k in candidate_votes) {
    Q[k + '_votes'] = Math.round(1000*candidate_votes[k]/total_votes)/10;
    Q[k + '_votes_disp'] = Q[k + '_votes'].toFixed(1);
}
Q.winner_votes = Math.round(1000*Q.winner_votes/total_votes)/10;
Q.winner_votes_disp = Q.winner_votes.toFixed(1);
Q.winner_desc = candidate_descs[Q.winner];

Q.round += 1

if (Q.marcher_candidate == "Boycott" || Q.sapd_candidate == "Boycott" || Q.collectivist_candidate == "Boycott") {
    Q.boycott_votes = 0;
    if (Q.collectivist_candidate == "Boycott") Q.boycott_votes += Q.collectivist_votes;
    if (Q.sapd_candidate == "Boycott") Q.boycott_votes += Q.sapd_votes;
    if (Q.marcher_candidate == "Boycott") Q.boycott_votes += Q.marcher_votes;
}
!}
go-to: r2_start if round = 1 and not has_majority; election_end if round > 1; r1_winner if has_majority

Election results:

[? if Gorrick_running : <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Gorrick**</span> - [+ Gorrick_votes_disp +]% ?]

[? if Strasser_running : <span style="color: #6A1E1E;">**Crowde**</span> - [+ Strasser_votes_disp +]% ?]

[? if Frick_running : <span style="color: #6A1E1E;">**Frask**</span> - [+ Frick_votes_disp +]% ?]

[? if Hammerstein_running : <span style="color: #BFC8CC;">**Hammerton**</span> - [+ Hammerstein_votes_disp +]% ?]

[? if Adenauer_running : <span style="color: #000000;">**Aldermoor**</span> - [+ Adenauer_votes_disp +]% ?]

[? if Heuss_running : [? if not lvp_formed: <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**Hewes**</span>?][? if lvp_formed: <span style="color: #FFCC00;">**Hewes**</span>?] - [+ Heuss_votes_disp +]% ?]

[? if Schumacher_running : <span style="color: #c00000;">**Shackley**</span> - [+ Schumacher_votes_disp +]% ?]

[? if marcher_candidate == "Boycott" or sapd_candidate == "Boycott" or collectivist_candidate == "Boycott" : Spoiled Ballots - [+ boycott_votes +]% ?]

@r2_start
on-arrival: {!
Q.adenauer_drops_out = 0;
Q.heuss_drops_out = 0;
if (Q.unionist_candidate == "Aldermoor" && (Q.ddp_candidate == "Hewes" || Q.gold_candidate == "Hewes" || Q.lvp_candidate == "Hewes") && Q.unionist_candidate != Q.marcher_candidate && (Q.ddp_candidate != Q.marcher_candidate || Q.gold_candidate != Q.marcher_candidate || Q.lvp_candidate != Q.marcher_candidate)) {
    if (Q.Adenauer_votes > Q.Heuss_votes) {
        Q.heuss_drops_out = 1;
        if (Q.ddp_candidate != Q.marcher_candidate && Q.ddp_candidate != Q.gnu_candidate) {
            Q.ddp_candidate = "Aldermoor";
        }
        if (Q.gold_candidate != Q.marcher_candidate && Q.gold_candidate != Q.gnu_candidate) {
            Q.gold_candidate = "Aldermoor";
        }
        if (Q.lvp_candidate != Q.marcher_candidate && Q.lvp_candidate != Q.gnu_candidate) {
            Q.lvp_candidate = "Aldermoor";
        }
    } else {
        Q.adenauer_drops_out = 1;
        Q.unionist_candidate = "Hewes";
    }
}
!}
go-to: r2_menu

In the lead is [+ winner_desc +]. There is no majority in the first round. In the second round, any candidate who wins a plurality will win overall.

The <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalists</span> and their splinter parties remain divided, locked in a permanent grudge. As a result, [+ dsu_candidate +] and [+ royalist_candidate +] will continue to run separately. Their inability to set aside mutual animosities signals the effective death of the movement, which spends more time quarreling internally than opposing the regime.

[? if heuss_drops_out : The liberal candidate Theodor Hewes has dropped out in favor of the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?]'s Konrad Aldermoor. This consolidates the votes of the moderate <i>Bürgerblock</i>, and they're expected to put up a decent fight against [+ gnu_candidate +]. ?]
[? if adenauer_drops_out : The [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] candidate Konrad Aldermoor has dropped out in favor of the liberal candidate Theodor Hewes. This consolidates the votes of the moderate <i>Bürgerblock</i>, and they're expected to put up a decent fight against [+ gnu_candidate +]. ?]

What should we do?

@r2_menu

- @r2_endorse_hammerstein: Support the <span style="color: #BFC8CC;">**GNU**</span>'s [+ gnu_candidate +].
- @r2_endorse_adenauer
- @r2_endorse_heuss
- @r2_campaigning: Can we convince any of the parties to change their endorsements?
- @r2_vote: Let the voting begin.

@r2_endorse_hammerstein
view-if: marcher_candidate != gnu_candidate and gnu_candidate == "Hammerton"
unavailable-subtitle: We are a democratic party. 
choose-if: staal_marcher_influence >= 8
on-arrival: marcher_candidate = gnu_candidate; collectivist_candidate = "Boycott"; sapd_candidate = "Boycott"
go-to: r1_menu

I hope you had a reason in mind.

@r2_endorse_adenauer
title: Switch our support to Konrad Aldermoor of the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?].
view-if: unionist_candidate = "Aldermoor" and marcher_candidate != unionist_candidate
on-departure: collectivist_candidate = "Boycott"; sapd_candidate = "Boycott"; marcher_candidate = "Aldermoor"; unionist_relation += 5; center_bvp_votes = 1 if unionist_relation < 50; is_unity_candidate = 1
go-to: r2_campaigning

We have endorsed Konrad Aldermoor of the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?]. Perhaps we can form a Unity Bloc against Staal.

[? if unionist_relation < 50 : With our support of Aldermoor, some of the most conservative parts of the <span style="color: #A2D8E0;">the Arcanists</span> have broken away from the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?], shifting their support to [+ gnu_candidate +]. Hopefully it doesn't lead to a repeat of the 4290 Presidential election. ?]

[? if collectivist_candidate = marcher_candidate: The <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span> is now breaking from our previous coalition and boycotting the election instead. ?]

@r2_endorse_heuss
title: Switch our support to Theodor Hewes.
view-if: (ddp_candidate = "Hewes" or lvp_candidate == "Hewes" or gold_candidate == "Hewes") and marcher_candidate != "Hewes"
on-departure: collectivist_candidate = "Boycott"; sapd_candidate = "Boycott"; marcher_candidate = "Hewes"; ddp_relation += 8; lvp_relation += 5; gold_candidate = gnu_candidate if gold_relation < 60 and gold_candidate == marcher_candidate and gold_exist and not lvp_formed; is_unity_candidate = 1
go-to: r2_campaigning

We have endorsed Theodor Hewes of the [? if not lvp_formed: <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span>?][? if lvp_formed: <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>?].

[? if gold_relation < 60 and gold_candidate == marcher_candidate and gold_exist and not lvp_formed: With our support of Hewes, the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span> components supporting him have broken away and are now supporting [+ gnu_candidate +] if they haven't already. ?]

[? if collectivist_candidate = marcher_candidate: The <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span> is now breaking from our previous coalition and boycotting the election instead. ?]

@r2_campaigning
