Kurt Shackley has won the presidency! This is a historic victory—how far we’ve come from the DuFour-backed Goodryke and Staal cabinets, all the way to a <span style="color: #c00000;">Reformist</span> president. Perhaps now, at last, we can begin to reform the Commonwealth, set it back on the right track, and undo the damage Staal inflicted during his year in office.

- @game_over: Game over.

@election_end
go-to: hammerstein_win if winner == "Hammerton" or winner == "Crowde" or winner == "Gorrick" or winner == "Gorrick" or winner == "Frask"; heuss_win if winner == "Hewes"; adenauer_win if winner == "Aldermoor"; schumacher_win if winner == "Shackley"
on-arrival: president = winner; president = "Hammerton" if (winner == "Crowde" or winner == "Gorrick" or winner == "Gorrick" or winner == "Frask")

The election has been won by [+ winner_desc +].
